Timex is a nice mac laptop, but it's firmly stuck at MacOS 14.
I need a way to extend the life as best I can.

!Updating Brew

```
$ brew update && brew upgrade
```
This used to run reliably, but now throws errors.
Some things cannot be installed, and some things are broken (like rpiwiki).

The error log suggests using MacPorts

!Updating Xcode
I was on Xcode 16.0 and the brew logs complained loudly, asking for Xcode 16.2.
After signing in with my apple credentials, I dug through apple website and eventually found Xcode 16.2 Command Line Tools:

```
https://developer.apple.com/download/all/?q=xcode
```

After installing that, Brew continued to report it was finding Xcode 16.0.
I deleted Applications/Xcode, installed the command line tools again, and brew complained.  
It really did want Xcode - the whole thing.

Back to that URL (above).  
Found Xcode 16.2.
It downloads as a ".xip" file, which it can decompress into Xcode folder -- in Downloads!
You need to copy ~/Downloads to /Applications/.
I think I also had to run Xcode once and have it install Xcode.
Doesn't make much sense to download a huge file, then have to run it to install stuff, but that's my memory.

Check your work:

```
$ xcodebuild -version
```

!MacPorts

macports.org

Apparently you can mix brew and macports, but the advice I saw was especially libraries can cause conflicts.
Perhaps use brew primary, then scan the logs to find errors that brew can't handle.
Uninstall whatever is causing heartburn with brew, install using macports.

More fiddling, but it may get me a usable machine again.

